Prepare test cases – Create test cases based on the project requirements.

Unit testing – Test individual modules or components separately.

Integration testing – Check whether different modules work correctly together.

System testing – Test the complete system as a whole.

Functional testing – Verify that all required features perform their intended functions.

Performance testing – Check the system's speed, stability, and response under different conditions.

Security testing – Check authentication, authorization, and protection of user data.

User acceptance testing (UAT) – Allow intended users to test the system and provide feedback.

Identify and fix bugs – Record errors, correct them, and test again.

Final validation – Confirm that the system satisfies the specified requirements.
